# Alerting rules for @{service}/@{objective_name} -- generated from the
# objective specification. Do not edit: the specification is the reviewed
# artifact and this file is rebuilt from it.
#
# Objective: @{title}
# Target:    @{target_rate} of valid events over @{window} (@{window_kind})
# Budget:    @{budget_rate} of events, equivalent to @{budget_span} of total failure
# Owner:     @{owner}
#
# Each tier is ONE rule with two conditions joined by `and`: the long window
# decides when it fires, the short window decides when it clears. Both sides
# carry the same threshold, which is the error rate the burn rate corresponds
# to for this objective -- not a figure chosen per window.
#
# The staleness rule is not a tier. No burn-rate expression can report its own
# missing denominator: when the series disappears every tier evaluates to
# nothing, and a rule over nothing does not fire.
